rem Randomly Decaying Sequence
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=697

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Nn integer = 10000000

rem -ln X(n) = ln c + the sum of n
rem exponentials, a Gamma(n, 1) sum S,
rem and X(n) < 1 means S > ln c. So ln c
rem is the 75% point of Gamma(n, 1), by
rem the Cornish-Fisher expansion at
rem z = 0.6744897501960817 (the 75%
rem point of the normal law):
rem   x = n + z sqrt(n) + (z^2 - 1) / 3
rem     + (z^3 - 7 z) / (36 sqrt(n))
rem     - (3 z^4 + 7 z^2 - 16)
rem       / (810 n).
rem The answer is x / ln 10.
Z = 0.6744897501960817
N = Nn * 1.0
Sr = N sqrt
X = N + Z * Sr + (Z * Z - 1.0) / 3.0
Z3 = Z * Z * Z
X = X + (Z3 - 7.0 * Z) / (36.0 * Sr)
Z2 = Z * Z
Q4 = 3.0 * Z2 * Z2 + 7.0 * Z2 - 16.0
X = X - Q4 / (810.0 * N)
Lg = X / 2.302585092994046
Answer = Lg text ".2f"
Answer print
